WEBVTT

00:08.908 --> 00:16.950
As a white, crescent moon overlooks the town

00:16.950 --> 00:24.948
From within a pale, blue maze
devilish things begin to stir

00:32.465 --> 00:36.269
Boy, here in this sinful world

00:36.269 --> 00:39.272
Believing, dreaming

00:39.272 --> 00:43.109
We are searching

00:43.109 --> 00:48.240
For the place to which souls should aspire

00:50.050 --> 00:58.458
Ah, how much profound darkness
must we turn to light

00:58.458 --> 01:03.029
For the color of the world to change?

01:03.029 --> 01:05.698
Ah, surely someday

01:05.698 --> 01:13.973
Ah, how many profound riddles must we solve

01:13.973 --> 01:18.933
For the door to paradise to open?

01:20.480 --> 01:27.113
Let's begin our journey

02:03.289 --> 02:08.818
The 5th Night
Challenge of the Mysterious Thief Frey!

02:09.195 --> 02:11.254
Mysterious thief, a mysterious thief!

02:11.898 --> 02:13.695
Mysterious Thief

02:13.766 --> 02:15.268
He sends out an announcement
before his robberies,

02:15.268 --> 02:16.769
then steals exactly what
he said he would.

02:16.769 --> 02:18.532
That is a mystery!

02:21.407 --> 02:23.409
The Mysterious Thief Frey, huh?

02:23.409 --> 02:24.277
Right!

02:24.277 --> 02:27.872
And it says the techniques he uses
have even the police baffled!

02:28.648 --> 02:33.176
The first things he stole were some
30,000,000 yen Lapis Lazuli gemstones.

02:33.820 --> 02:36.380
The next thing he took was an opal.

02:37.257 --> 02:39.759
Even though the police set up
some really tight security,

02:39.759 --> 02:42.193
he stole all of it easily,
just like he said he would.

02:42.462 --> 02:44.362
Is that awesome or what?

02:45.431 --> 02:47.922
And... What do you want
me to do about it?

02:48.234 --> 02:49.895
It's obvious, isn't it?

02:49.969 --> 02:54.133
We'll be the ones to capture the
"Mysterious Thief Frey"!

02:55.542 --> 02:56.709
Why me?

02:56.709 --> 02:59.212
You're a detective, right?

02:59.212 --> 03:01.510
So you've gotta go up against
the mysterious thief!

03:02.615 --> 03:03.673
Why?

03:04.384 --> 03:07.683
The Fiend with Twenty Faces
vs. Kogoro Akechi!

03:08.154 --> 03:10.179
Lupin vs. Holmes!

03:10.456 --> 03:13.560
Mysterious thieves and detectives
have always fought one another!

03:13.560 --> 03:15.428
Everyone knows that!

03:15.428 --> 03:17.263
Is that right?

03:17.263 --> 03:19.322
No. It isn't.

03:19.999 --> 03:23.298
Okay, we're off to catch Frey!

03:23.636 --> 03:25.103
I'm not going.

03:27.006 --> 03:28.508
Why?

03:28.508 --> 03:30.944
If he's deliberately increasing the
chances of his getting caught

03:30.944 --> 03:34.311
by announcing his robberies,
then he's just looking for attention.

03:35.148 --> 03:38.584
The more of a fuss people make
over him, the happier he is.

03:38.918 --> 03:41.287
But, he's a mysterious thief!

03:41.287 --> 03:44.256
It's better to just avoid
those types altogether.

03:46.259 --> 03:47.783
Okay, fine!

03:48.995 --> 03:52.396
I should just go catch Frey
on my own, right?!

03:56.669 --> 03:58.796
Are you all right with this, Master Loki?

03:59.239 --> 04:00.506
Yeah.

04:00.506 --> 04:03.276
If he's just some criminal who gets off
on the shock he causes,

04:03.276 --> 04:05.111
it's got nothing to do with
the evil we deal with.

04:05.111 --> 04:05.278
The Mysterious Thief Frey
it's got nothing to do with
the evil we deal with.

04:05.278 --> 04:05.778
The Mysterious Thief Frey

04:05.778 --> 04:07.580
The Mysterious Thief Frey
The Mysterious Thief Frey, huh?

04:09.082 --> 04:10.208
Frey?

04:10.850 --> 04:12.283
It couldn't be...

04:12.352 --> 04:14.020
Koh-i-Noor
The British
Crown Jewel
Coming to Japan!

04:14.020 --> 04:15.112
The British
Crown Jewel

04:15.455 --> 04:17.490
What's Loki's problem anyhow?

04:17.490 --> 04:20.823
I was all ready to go capture
the mystery thief with him!

04:23.997 --> 04:26.329
If that's the way it is,
then I swear that I'll...

04:32.171 --> 04:33.706
Oh, excuse me!

04:33.706 --> 04:35.333
Are you okay?

04:35.708 --> 04:36.834
I'm okay.

04:37.543 --> 04:39.010
I'm all...

04:39.879 --> 04:41.346
I'm sorry!

04:42.615 --> 04:44.384
I really am sorry about that.

04:44.384 --> 04:47.717
I was lost in my own thoughts, and...

04:54.894 --> 04:57.454
Does your cheek hurt?

04:58.731 --> 05:00.800
It... It's all right!

05:00.800 --> 05:02.062
See?

05:02.268 --> 05:03.565
Thank goodness.

05:04.070 --> 05:07.607
Um, actually, if you have the time,
maybe we could go get some tea or...

05:07.607 --> 05:09.302
Sorry to have bothered you.

05:12.178 --> 05:13.475
Your handkerchief!

05:13.780 --> 05:16.248
Keep it. Please feel free to use it.

05:24.590 --> 05:25.992
I've found her.

05:25.992 --> 05:29.529
Beautiful, intelligent, and
overflowing with warmth...

05:29.529 --> 05:32.225
A maternal instinct as well
as wits and glamor.

05:32.532 --> 05:35.301
She's exactly what I've been looking for...

05:35.301 --> 05:37.030
The classic Japanese beauty!

05:40.073 --> 05:41.438
Koh-i-Noor
The British
Crown Jewel
Coming to Japan!

05:41.507 --> 05:44.442
Great
Treasures
Exhibit

05:46.346 --> 05:47.813
The Mysterious Thief Frey!

05:49.148 --> 05:53.278
Damn it! He stole the Koh-i-Noor
just like he said he would!

05:56.289 --> 05:58.416
Yet another tremendous success!

05:58.891 --> 06:01.519
Nothing is impossible for the great Frey!

06:08.868 --> 06:11.070
My right eye is throbbing...

06:11.070 --> 06:14.972
It's throbbing, telling me to kill Loki.

06:19.212 --> 06:21.077
So you're back, Frey?

06:27.487 --> 06:30.223
Why draw this ridiculous
farce out any longer?

06:30.223 --> 06:32.350
It would all be over if you
just finished Loki off.

06:33.126 --> 06:35.754
Heimdall, don't get so worked up.

06:36.362 --> 06:39.098
The battle of the gods is a glorious thing.

06:39.098 --> 06:41.066
We must conduct it in an
intellectual manner.

06:41.401 --> 06:42.602
Shut up!

06:42.602 --> 06:47.039
My desire for revenge will not
be sated until Loki is dead!

06:47.473 --> 06:49.771
I swear I will kill him!

06:51.944 --> 06:53.571
Yeah, right.

06:54.080 --> 06:57.641
I came here because I heard you were
having a hard time of things.

06:57.984 --> 07:03.445
Just relax. You'll have your revenge.

07:04.824 --> 07:06.492
And I'll be the one to deliver it.

07:06.492 --> 07:08.187
Then do it now!

07:08.628 --> 07:10.496
Don't lose your head.

07:10.496 --> 07:12.765
When I announce my next target,

07:12.765 --> 07:15.563
I can most certainly expect
Loki to show up too.

07:16.302 --> 07:17.929
And then...

07:18.504 --> 07:21.473
Your next target? What's that?

07:23.309 --> 07:25.044
Ah, that's right.

07:25.044 --> 07:27.342
I have one other task for tonight.

07:28.047 --> 07:29.776
Well then, Heimdall.

07:30.616 --> 07:31.784
Adieu.

07:31.784 --> 07:34.912
I'm the one who's going to kill Loki!

07:38.724 --> 07:41.488
Lapis lazuli, opal...

07:43.296 --> 07:45.924
And now the Koh-i-Noor, huh?

07:46.199 --> 07:47.400
More, please!

07:47.400 --> 07:49.769
So you like it, Mr. Narugami?

07:49.769 --> 07:53.539
Yeah! You sure are good at
cooking, Four Eyes!

07:53.539 --> 07:55.875
Well, I'm glad it's to your liking.

07:55.875 --> 07:58.742
This kelp roll goes great with rice!

07:58.945 --> 08:03.516
That's because I'm using fresh
Shiretoko kelp I got via mail order.

08:03.516 --> 08:06.576
Man, you sure know your stuff!
I could eat a million of these!

08:09.655 --> 08:12.525
Jeez, didn't you learn anything
about what they call

08:12.525 --> 08:14.760
"restraint" before coming to this world?

08:14.760 --> 08:16.523
You say something, Loki?

08:17.296 --> 08:19.992
Nope. Nothing at all.

08:22.668 --> 08:24.637
That's excellent, Ecchan!

08:24.637 --> 08:28.971
Why did you name that familiar "Ecchan"?

08:29.575 --> 08:31.202
Excellent... - chan... Ecchan! Get it?

08:32.011 --> 08:35.139
A far cry from some good-for-nothing
freeloading I can think of.

08:36.082 --> 08:38.251
More, please! And a bigger
serving this time!

08:38.251 --> 08:42.688
By the way, we haven't seen much
of Mayura lately, have we?

08:43.289 --> 08:44.724
I wonder if she really is out on her own,

08:44.724 --> 08:47.159
pursuing that "Mysterious Thief Frey,"
or whatever.

08:47.159 --> 08:49.252
Don't know. Couldn't tell you.

08:50.196 --> 08:52.899
You've been checking the newspapers
regularly since she left,

08:52.899 --> 08:55.067
so I thought you might have been concerned...

08:55.067 --> 08:55.601
Oh! Thank you!
So I thought you might have been concerned...

08:55.601 --> 08:56.269
Oh! Thank you!

08:56.269 --> 09:00.228
Reading the newspaper is something
any detective does.

09:01.340 --> 09:02.942
It's got nothing to do with Mayura.

09:02.942 --> 09:04.136
Oh, really?

09:05.578 --> 09:06.636
Yes, really...

09:07.313 --> 09:09.181
No way! Could it be?

09:09.181 --> 09:11.376
What's the matter, Master Loki?

09:14.854 --> 09:18.290
The Brising necklace... but why?

09:20.293 --> 09:24.564
I'm sorry to bother you with this
when you're not feeling well.

09:24.564 --> 09:28.125
Nah, it's nothing!
I owe your dad a lot!

09:29.635 --> 09:32.271
Are you sure you're all right,
Inspector Niyama?

09:32.271 --> 09:33.906
Don't worry!

09:33.906 --> 09:37.510
I was up late last night,
inspecting the scene.

09:37.510 --> 09:40.411
A little cold like this isn't
enough to stop a det...

09:41.814 --> 09:45.147
By scene, do you mean the place where
the Koh-i-Noor was stolen?

09:45.484 --> 09:50.649
Yeah. And they stole a steel girder
from the construction site too.

09:50.890 --> 09:53.154
A steel girder? Frey did?

09:56.696 --> 09:58.731
But why a steel girder?

09:58.731 --> 09:59.966
Heck if I know.

09:59.966 --> 10:02.594
I've got no idea what that thief is thinking.

10:04.437 --> 10:07.139
Uh, Inspector! Your nose is running.

10:07.139 --> 10:08.902
Wait here just a second, okay?

10:15.548 --> 10:17.016
No one...

10:17.016 --> 10:19.685
No one is taking them!

10:19.685 --> 10:22.779
Are human beings really such
cold-hearted creatures?

10:23.089 --> 10:25.614
Excuse me! Could I have
some tissues, please?

10:26.192 --> 10:28.160
Sure! Take as many as you...

10:33.032 --> 10:35.125
You're that classic Japanese
beauty from before!

10:35.501 --> 10:36.866
Oh, it's you!

10:37.536 --> 10:41.440
Yes, you are the only true beauty of Japan.

10:41.440 --> 10:43.743
As long as there are such
gorgeous people as you around,

10:43.743 --> 10:46.541
there is still hope for the
world of mankind.

10:47.179 --> 10:49.248
Um... A pack of tissues, please?

10:49.248 --> 10:52.376
Yes, of course! Have as you like!

10:53.719 --> 10:55.812
And in return, could you please
tell me your name...

11:00.826 --> 11:03.852
Such grace is also a quality of
the classic Japanese beauty.

11:04.163 --> 11:07.326
It seems my eyes had not
deceived me after all.

11:07.733 --> 11:09.702
Sorry about that, Mayura.

11:09.702 --> 11:10.498
Huh?

11:11.637 --> 11:12.471
8th Floor
So humans aren't allowed to steal, huh?
Well, since it's okay for a GOD to,
I'll be helping myself to the
Brising necklace tomorrow
at 11:00 pm.
The Mysterious Thief Frey

11:12.471 --> 11:16.942
8th Floor
So humans aren't allowed to steal, huh?
Well, since it's okay for a GOD to,
I'll be helping myself to the
Brising necklace tomorrow
at 11:00 pm.
The Mysterious Thief Frey
"I'll be helping myself to the Brising
necklace tomorrow at 11:00 pm.

11:16.942 --> 11:18.644
8th Floor
So humans aren't allowed to steal, huh?
Well, since it's okay for a GOD to,
I'll be helping myself to the
Brising necklace tomorrow
at 11:00 pm.
The Mysterious Thief Frey
The Mysterious Thief, Frey"?

11:19.445 --> 11:21.681
This is Frey's announcement?!

11:21.681 --> 11:23.916
Don't tell me that the guy
from before was...

11:23.916 --> 11:25.317
Damn him!

11:25.317 --> 11:28.287
Waltzing out in broad daylight and
leaving his announcements...

11:28.287 --> 11:30.790
But why on packs of tissues?

11:30.790 --> 11:31.882
I dunno!

11:32.892 --> 11:36.162
What is the Brising necklace doing
here in the human world?

11:36.162 --> 11:38.097
Could she be here too?

11:38.097 --> 11:41.589
Then that "Mysterious Thief Frey" is also...

11:42.401 --> 11:44.503
Loki! I've got big news!

11:44.503 --> 11:48.633
Frey says he's going to steal
the Brising necklace next!

11:48.941 --> 11:50.408
What did you say?!

11:51.811 --> 11:53.145
What was that?

11:53.145 --> 11:54.840
It came from the foyer!

11:59.952 --> 12:01.920
What in the world?

12:02.254 --> 12:05.491
This could be the steel girder
that Frey stole!

12:05.491 --> 12:06.685
Frey?

12:09.895 --> 12:11.522
I see.

12:12.231 --> 12:16.031
Frey, is this your way of challenging me?

12:28.614 --> 12:32.914
There's a message in the items Frey
stole and in the order he did it.

12:33.552 --> 12:35.688
What do you mean, Loki?

12:35.688 --> 12:37.849
It's like this...

12:38.791 --> 12:41.760
The first item stolen was lapis lazuli.

12:42.061 --> 12:44.529
Spell out its mineral component
in English, and you have...

12:45.297 --> 12:47.788
The next thing he stole was was opal...

12:49.168 --> 12:51.670
After that, the Koh-i-Noor.

12:51.670 --> 12:55.629
Lastly, he stole a steel girder,
which is made from iron.

12:57.877 --> 13:00.446
Take the first letter from each of
those words and it spells...

13:00.446 --> 13:03.315
L-O-K-I...

13:03.315 --> 13:04.483
Loki!

13:04.483 --> 13:07.219
I get it, it spells your name!

13:07.219 --> 13:10.589
Which means that in stealing these items,

13:10.589 --> 13:13.459
Frey was really issuing a challenge to me.

13:13.459 --> 13:16.328
But, how does Frey know you?

13:16.328 --> 13:17.955
Well...

13:19.632 --> 13:21.099
Loki?

13:21.934 --> 13:25.204
It's because Loki is a famous detective.

13:25.204 --> 13:27.573
Oh, I get it!

13:27.573 --> 13:29.871
Well, we're almost at the museum.

13:34.713 --> 13:38.149
Kakinouchi
Museum

13:43.189 --> 13:46.492
The police have certainly pulled
all the stops this time, huh?

13:46.492 --> 13:51.930
A police troop like this won't be
any use against Frey.

13:52.298 --> 13:54.766
Huh? Daidoji, is that you?

13:57.536 --> 14:00.539
Kotaro! What are you doing here?

14:00.539 --> 14:04.376
Hey now, let's not forget this
museum is privately owned

14:04.376 --> 14:06.478
by the Kakinouchi Corporation.

14:06.478 --> 14:09.882
The Kakinouchi Corporation?
You mean like that famous company?

14:09.882 --> 14:12.908
Kotaro, does this mean
your family is rich?

14:13.719 --> 14:16.655
It's not such a big deal.

14:16.655 --> 14:20.921
My parents' money has
nothing to do with me.

14:21.327 --> 14:23.955
Let's be pals, okay?

14:25.731 --> 14:27.733
Who's this, Mayura?

14:27.733 --> 14:30.102
Kotaro Kakenouchi.

14:30.102 --> 14:32.771
He goes to the same school as me.

14:32.771 --> 14:34.974
And he's totally rich!

14:34.974 --> 14:37.109
Who is that, Daidoji?

14:37.109 --> 14:39.378
Loki. He's a detective.

14:39.378 --> 14:40.606
A detective?

14:41.247 --> 14:43.442
I am Loki, from the
Enjaku Detective Agency.

14:45.618 --> 14:47.987
Is the necklace in the display room?

14:47.987 --> 14:50.389
Yeah, it's that way.

14:50.389 --> 14:51.686
Follow me.

14:52.491 --> 14:56.629
Hey, Yamino, don't those two
kind of resemble each other?

14:56.629 --> 14:59.462
Yes, well, they certainly give off
that sort of feel.

15:20.920 --> 15:22.217
Wow...

15:22.922 --> 15:25.391
What a beautiful goddess.

15:25.391 --> 15:27.559
I wonder what exactly
she's the goddess of.

15:27.559 --> 15:30.687
This is Freya, a goddess
from Norse mythology.

15:32.631 --> 15:35.429
She's the goddess of beauty,
fertility and love.

15:41.373 --> 15:43.933
The Brising necklace...

15:45.277 --> 15:48.113
Where and how did you come
upon this necklace?

15:48.113 --> 15:52.550
I'm not sure. I heard it just came up
on auction somewhere.

15:53.118 --> 15:56.922
Supposedly, no one has any idea
who owned it before that.

15:56.922 --> 15:58.389
I see.

16:00.125 --> 16:01.860
That's very odd.

16:01.860 --> 16:05.931
It's not the kind of item that would
just show up out of the blue.

16:05.931 --> 16:06.898
Yeah...

16:23.649 --> 16:25.549
Loki! Check it out!

16:27.019 --> 16:30.511
Now I'll catch the Mysterious
Thief Frey for sure!

16:30.856 --> 16:32.380
Um, Mayura...

16:34.059 --> 16:34.159
Our rice is hot and steamy and
our nori is crispy and fresh!

16:34.159 --> 16:36.562
Best Onigiri
Under the Sun
Our rice is hot and steamy and
our nori is crispy and fresh!

16:36.562 --> 16:36.729
Our rice is hot and steamy and
our nori is crispy and fresh!

16:36.729 --> 16:37.629
It's the Mysterious Thief Frey!
Our rice is hot and steamy and
our nori is crispy and fresh!

16:37.629 --> 16:39.164
It's the Mysterious Thief Frey!
Best Onigiri Under the Sun at your service!

16:39.164 --> 16:39.892
Best Onigiri Under the Sun at your service!

16:44.336 --> 16:46.395
What the heck are you doing?!

17:20.239 --> 17:23.470
Damn it... This is Frey's work.

17:27.112 --> 17:31.116
The heavens call out, the Earth calls out,
the people call out.

17:31.116 --> 17:34.253
They call upon me to defeat him!

17:34.253 --> 17:37.056
See for yourselves, for tonight I have come.

17:37.056 --> 17:40.759
Bathed in beautiful moonlight,
I descend from the land of the gods.

17:40.759 --> 17:43.387
Beauty unparalleled... Omnipotent...

17:44.430 --> 17:46.432
Invincible...

17:46.432 --> 17:50.836
The magnificent, Mysterious
Thief Frey, is before you!

17:50.836 --> 17:52.804
You bastard...

17:54.940 --> 17:57.272
By the way, where is Loki?

18:01.547 --> 18:04.607
It seems he has run away in fear of me.

18:06.852 --> 18:08.479
Well, small wonder.

18:11.290 --> 18:12.689
Too easy.

18:13.092 --> 18:16.186
This isn't entertaining at all.

18:19.832 --> 18:22.134
What is the meaning of this!

18:22.134 --> 18:24.102
It's been a while, hasn't it Frey?

18:26.171 --> 18:28.867
So you've finally shown yourself, Loki!

18:29.241 --> 18:30.609
Frey...

18:30.609 --> 18:34.146
A "Mysterious Thief," eh?
As unpredictable as always, aren't you?

18:34.146 --> 18:40.278
And you're absurd as ever, showing up
in the guise of a child.

18:40.886 --> 18:43.184
That's not something I want
to hear from you.

18:43.655 --> 18:45.782
Why have you come to the human world?

18:46.892 --> 18:48.951
You will fight me, Loki!

18:49.995 --> 18:50.996
Why?

18:50.996 --> 18:54.299
Because mysterious thieves and detectives
always fight each other!

18:54.299 --> 18:57.598
That's why I've tried so hard
to be a mysterious thief!

18:58.604 --> 19:01.095
Are you on the same level
as Mayura or what?

19:01.773 --> 19:05.607
Have you also come to kill me
by Odin's orders?

19:07.346 --> 19:10.349
I would do nothing so uncivilized!

19:10.349 --> 19:12.518
So it's not by Odin's order?

19:12.518 --> 19:17.251
Even if it were, I still have my
own way of doing them!

19:17.723 --> 19:18.849
And...

19:19.124 --> 19:20.250
And?

19:22.528 --> 19:24.596
I have one more question.

19:24.596 --> 19:29.090
Since the Brising necklace is here,
could it be that...

19:29.468 --> 19:31.333
Come forth, Gullinbursti!

19:33.372 --> 19:34.498
What?!

19:38.577 --> 19:41.513
Sorry, but this is for my
sister's sake too.

19:41.513 --> 19:43.344
I won't hand over this necklace.

19:43.649 --> 19:46.083
So Freya really is here?!

19:46.685 --> 19:48.516
I needn't answer that!

19:49.721 --> 19:51.120
You're not getting away!

19:57.863 --> 19:59.330
Up here, Loki!

20:02.701 --> 20:04.603
If you want this necklace,

20:04.603 --> 20:07.265
then show me your talents and
steal it from the great Frey!

20:09.174 --> 20:11.039
Go, Gullinbursti!

20:16.615 --> 20:21.416
How absurd to think you could beat me
with that child's body!

20:25.991 --> 20:27.793
Come then, what's the matter?

20:27.793 --> 20:31.695
Revert to your original form
and fight me, Loki!

20:40.405 --> 20:42.202
In that case, it's time to finish you off!

20:45.811 --> 20:47.938
I found you, Mysterious Thief Frey!

20:48.747 --> 20:52.251
I figured since you're a thief,
you'd escape to the roof for sure!

20:52.251 --> 20:54.353
I even set up an ambush!

20:54.353 --> 20:57.089
But what are you doing on that roof?!

20:57.089 --> 21:00.225
Ah, why if it isn't my little
Japanese beauty!

21:00.225 --> 21:02.819
So you've come to see me, have you?

21:04.263 --> 21:05.958
Wait there! I'll be right...

21:07.599 --> 21:09.501
How did this happen?!

21:09.501 --> 21:10.798
The necklace!

21:13.572 --> 21:14.840
Heimdall!

21:14.840 --> 21:16.308
Very sneaky!

21:16.308 --> 21:20.612
But next time I'll be sure to
tear you to pieces!

21:20.612 --> 21:22.273
Until then, Loki!

21:22.581 --> 21:23.682
Frey...

21:23.682 --> 21:26.276
Stop right there, Mysterious Thief Frey!

21:26.818 --> 21:28.954
Oh, hey there, my little
Japanese beauty!

21:28.954 --> 21:31.047
Next time, why don't we both
go out for tea or...

21:36.228 --> 21:38.128
Frey?

22:16.968 --> 22:28.937
A moonlit road pierces the dense fog

22:30.649 --> 22:42.394
Perplexedly, we all wander towards tomorrow

22:42.394 --> 22:49.501
We escape the darkness of a desolate town

22:49.501 --> 22:55.941
Which threatens to halt even the telling of myths

22:55.941 --> 23:05.450
Transcending the limitless skies,
we're on a journey

23:05.450 --> 23:09.788
Even if we're hurt

23:09.788 --> 23:21.800
We're sure we can still make it,
so we want to keep on praying

23:21.800 --> 23:23.529
Believe in Heaven

